    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "At the same speed, crossing time grows in the same ratio as train length.\n\nIf a 120 m train takes 6 s to clear a pole, then a 180 m train at the same speed is 1.5 times as long, so it takes 1.5 × 6 = 9 s.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_6_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_6_step": {
      "id": "teach_6_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "You can use proportional thinking without finding the speed at all:\n\ntime₂/time₁ = length₂/length₁\n\nThis is faster when the speed is explicitly the same.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_6"
        }
      ]
    },
