    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The chapter also hides simple distance counting inside train stories. Suppose pillars stand every 100 m. If a train covers 6000 m, there are 6000/100 = 60 gaps between the first and last pillar.\n\nBut the number of pillars is 61 because both ends count.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
