      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now connect the ideas. A train at 48 km/hr crosses a pole in 9 s.\n\n48 km/hr = 40/3 m/s, so its length is (40/3) × 9 = 120 m.\nIf it next meets a 180 m platform, the crossing distance becomes 120 + 180 = 300 m.",
